Usage: agent-deck [-p profile] conductor setup <name> [options]

Set up a named conductor: creates its directory, instructions file, meta.json, and session registration.
Multiple conductors can exist per profile.

Arguments:
  <name>    Conductor name (e.g., ryan, infra, monitor)

Options:
  -agent string
        Conductor agent runtime: claude, codex, hermes, or pi (default "claude")
  -description string
        Description for this conductor
  -heartbeat
        Enable heartbeat for this conductor (default)
  -no-heartbeat
        Disable heartbeat for this conductor
  -heartbeat-idle-minutes int
        Minutes of idle time before pausing heartbeats (default 0=disabled, negative also disabled)
  -no-clear-on-compact
        Claude-only: allow normal compaction instead of /clear when context fills up
        The /clear only arms on an established context window (AGENTDECK_CONTEXT_WINDOW
        or a harness-reported size); a window inferred from the model id leaves it off.

Conductor-specific files:
  -instructions-md string
        Custom instructions file for this conductor (agent-specific)
  -claude-md string
        Deprecated Claude-only alias for -instructions-md
  -policy-md string
        Custom POLICY.md for this conductor (e.g., ~/docs/my-policy.md)
  -heartbeat-rules-md string
        Custom HEARTBEAT_RULES.md for this conductor (e.g., ~/docs/my-heartbeat-rules.md)

Shared files (all conductors):
  -shared-instructions-md string
        Custom shared instructions file for all conductors of this agent
  -shared-claude-md string
        Deprecated Claude-only alias for -shared-instructions-md
  -shared-policy-md string
        Custom path for shared POLICY.md (e.g., ~/docs/conductor-policy.md)

Environment:
  -env KEY=VALUE
        Environment variable for the conductor session (can be repeated)
  -env-file string
        Path to .env file to source before conductor starts

Output:
  -json
        Output as JSON
